cff-version: 1.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "UAV Multispectral YOLO: Automated Agricultural Imagery Mapping on Edge Devices"
authors:
  -  "Jino Joy", "Ajay Singh", "Kelvin Betitame", "Kirk Howatt", "Joseph Mettler", "William Aderholdt", "Xin Sun"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jinojoy123/uav-multispectral-yolo"
url: "https://github.com/jinojoy123/uav-multispectral-yolo"
abstract: >-
  Research framework for RGB and five-band RGBRN (Red, Green, Blue,
  Red Edge, and Near-Infrared) YOLO instance segmentation of UAV
  agricultural imagery. The repository includes modified Ultralytics
  implementations for YOLO, model training and
  evaluation scripts, TensorRT export and testing, and orthomosaic-based
  mapping workflows for NVIDIA Jetson Orin edge devices. Sugarbeet
  and weed segmentation and prescription mapping are the demonstrated
  agricultural application.
keywords:
  - multispectral imaging
  - unmanned aerial vehicle
  - YOLO
  - instance segmentation
  - edge computing
  - NVIDIA Jetson
  - precision agriculture
  - weed mapping
license: AGPL-3.0-only
